# Byte-exact recorded upstream responses.
#
# The Go checksum-database signed note is verified by computing an Ed25519
# signature over the note text's *exact bytes*, including its LF line endings.
# Git's autocrlf would rewrite LF -> CRLF on Windows checkout, corrupting the
# signed text so verification fails (tc_110_02 / tc_110_03). Treat the fixture
# as binary so it is never EOL-converted on any platform. See task 110.
tests/fixtures/go_sumdb_real/** -text

# The published version pin is a byte-exact, LF-terminated channel (served
# verbatim over raw.githubusercontent and asserted byte-for-byte by
# tests/version_pin_integration.rs t113_02/t113_03). Git's autocrlf rewrites
# LF -> CRLF on Windows checkout, corrupting it to "v1.3.1\r\n" and failing CI
# on Windows only. Force LF on every platform. See task 113 (same class as the
# task-110 go_sumdb fixture guard above).
PINNED_VERSION text eol=lf
